# TinyHTTP

TinyHTTP is a tiny HTTP server built from scratch in C# using raw TCP sockets.

This project started as a backend/networking learning project and evolved into a practical cybersecurity playground used to explore:
- TCP connections
- HTTP requests and responses
- Network communication
- Request parsing
- Routing
- Input handling
- Server behavior
- Security concepts

The goal of TinyHTTP is not to compete with production web servers, but to deeply understand what happens underneath modern frameworks.

---

# Why This Project Exists

Most beginner projects focus on CRUD applications like student managers or library systems.

TinyHTTP takes a different approach.

Instead of only building business logic, this project focuses on understanding:
- how browsers communicate with servers,
- how HTTP works,
- how requests are processed,
- how responses are generated,
- and how backend systems can become attack surfaces.

This project is also being used as a practical learning environment for networking and cybersecurity concepts.

---

# Current Features

- TCP server using TcpListener
- Browser connection handling
- HTTP request reading
- HTTP response sending
- Basic route handling
- Console request logging
- Asynchronous communication using async/await

---

