---

# What I Learned So Far

- Everything sent over a network eventually becomes bytes.
- Browsers communicate with servers using HTTP requests.
- TcpListener waits for incoming connections.
- TcpClient represents an active connection.
- NetworkStream carries data between client and server.
- HTTP headers tell browsers how to interpret incoming data.
- Servers must carefully handle external input.

---

# Running The Project

## Requirements
- .NET SDK installed
- Visual Studio or VS Code

## Run

```bash
dotnet run
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

